Hinkin (1995)
- Item Generation: 2 approaches were described
(1) Deduction approach ("logical partitioning"/"classification from above") -- theoretically driven
-- understand construct 
-- thorough research on the construct of interest
-- creation of a definition
-- definition is used as a guide to generate items
(2) Inductive approach ("grouping" / "classification from below")
-- asking individuals to provide descriptions or feelings, describe behaviors
-- content analysis categories/classifications based on themes or key words
-- items are then put into a sorting process (pretest)

